commit c1279721dee3d3cdce3f0a3f8e7e701dcb1bb06e
Author: Satheesh Kumar <satheesh.kumar@ittiam.com>
Date:   Wed Dec 20 15:17:10 2023 +0530

    Fix the potential leaks and SEGV error from row_mt_mem_alloc()

    In row_mt_mem_alloc(), if the allocations related to
    'this_tile->row_mt_sync' or 'this_tile->row_ctx' fails in one of the
    tiles, 'enc_row_mt->allocated_tile_cols' and
    'enc_row_mt->allocated_tile_rows' will not be set due to the longjmp
    and the allocated buffers will show up as leaks. This CL fixes this
    issue by setting these variables before the allocation. These buffers
    are also initialized to NULL in av1_alloc_tile_data() to fix the SEGV
    error when av1_row_mt_mem_dealloc() is invoked in case of an
    allocation failure.

    Bug: aomedia:3276
    Change-Id: I9d2ddd2b22e1dff5450d9f052ed5a16dba0a7cf1

 av1/decoder/decodeframe.c   |  1 +
 av1/decoder/decoder.c       |  2 ++
